- A genuinely repeatable event can be counted only when the text semantics support repetition AND the event times differ under the time-source priority above. Repeatable actions include buying, visiting, traveling, eating, attending or participating in seminars/events, meeting people, taking classes, shopping, and exercising. Singular wording alone does not make such an action a one-off event.
- When two occurrences are established, state the exact count `twice`; when three are established, state `three times`, and so on. Put the count in the output even when dates are also listed, for example `The user visited Rome twice, on 2024-03-01 and 2024-03-10.` Never use only `again`, `another time`, or a list of dates without the exact count.
